# Subjects discovered at runtime. This *was* treated as a regenerable cache
# and left untracked -- correct while the product only ran locally, where a
# rebuilt subject persists on disk.
#
# Deployment changed the calculus. A free Render instance resets its
# filesystem on every spin-down (15 idle minutes), so a subject built in
# production survives only until the next quiet quarter-hour. Shipping the
# corpus inside the image is what makes an uncurated subject open instantly
# instead of costing a visitor two minutes for something that will not last.
#
# So it is committed deliberately: a pinned demo corpus, not a cache. Live
# building still works on top of it, and `store.clear()` still rebuilds it.
backend/tests/_test_generated/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Demo render output
demo/audio/
*.mp4

# Root-level planning/notes docs: kept locally as working references, not
# part of the published repo. README stays -- it's the front door.
# (PROJECT_GUIDE.md -- the full architecture-and-flow explainer -- is covered
# by this wildcard; named explicitly too so the intent survives a future edit.)
/*.md
!/README.md
/PROJECT_GUIDE.md

# The problem-statement PDF: reference material, not part of the repo.
/*.pdf

# Claude Code project config: local dev-server launch settings, not shared.
.claude/
